> Docs\VOICE.md:31:## Triggers
  Docs\VOICE.md:32:
  Docs\VOICE.md:33:Existing: `stageStart`, `prepRefused`, `holdCommitted`, `demobCommitted`, `orderLanded`, 
`orderNotDone`, `conflict`, `heldDay1` to `heldDay3`, `stageEnd`.
  Docs\VOICE.md:34:
  Docs\VOICE.md:35:New in WO-S10:
  Docs\VOICE.md:36:- `event` with `eventType` (P1, A2, ...): a foreman's reaction where the event happens.
  Docs\VOICE.md:37:- `arrive` with `crew` and `status`: Site stands within 30 m of that crew; at most once per crew 
per day. For `working` this is the everyday chatter that can hide a deviation.
  Docs\VOICE.md:38:- `sky` with `state` (`towersSouth`): a foreman remarks on the weather when it turns.
  Docs\VOICE.md:39:- `holdPoint` with `zone`: the backfill foreman reaches a zone end and asks for the sign-off.
  Docs\VOICE.md:40:- `conflict` with `pair` (`back-pipe`, `pipe-exc`) and `cause` (`caughtUp`, `leaderStopped`, 
`leaderWaiting`): the argument. The most specific match wins (pair and cause, then pair, then any).
  Docs\VOICE.md:41:- `conflictRepeat` with `pair`: a two-line grumble when a trailing crew catches its leader again 
after the first argument.
  Docs\VOICE.md:42:
  Docs\VOICE.md:43:A line is either one `text` with a `speaker`, or an exchange `turns: [{speaker, text}, ...]` played 
in order from each speaker's position, 0.3 s apart.
  Docs\VOICE.md:44:
> Docs\VOICE.md:45:## Arguments (O12, expanded)
  Docs\VOICE.md:46:
  Docs\VOICE.md:47:1. The first argument of each crew pair in a stage stops both crews and is a four-turn exchange 
(K7, unchanged).
  Docs\VOICE.md:48:2. Arguments also fire when the trailing crew catches a leader that is waiting at an unposted 
permit boundary or a hold point. The projection uses the leader's actual movement over the last hour of simulated time 
instead of its machine rate. Holding permits too tightly then has a voice: the pipe crew catches the parked excavator, 
and the two foremen argue about the paper.
  Docs\VOICE.md:49:3. After the first argument, a trailing crew that catches up again triggers a two-line grumble 
(`conflictRepeat`) without stopping anything, at most once a day per pair.
  Docs\VOICE.md:50:4. The numbers that matter (rates, days, stations) are spoken in the argument, never shown on a 
screen.
  Docs\VOICE.md:51:
