> Docs\VOICE.md:98:How the sheet follows the principles: Marcus at the collapse gives the station, the water and his 
refusal, not the clearing days or the options. The argument carries the rates (250 against 180) and the blame on the 
schedule, which is the push lesson, for Plan to find on the LOB. Ray's morning line is the deviation tell. Marcus's 
sky line points at open trench without a number; Rules counts the tokens. Dana's hold-point line claims two of the 
three checklist items, which Site must see for itself, and the third (compaction) is only in Plan's inbox.
  Docs\VOICE.md:99:
> Docs\VOICE.md:100:## Not now
  Docs\VOICE.md:101:
> Docs\VOICE.md:102:A live voice agent (players question a foreman and an LLM answers in character) would sharpen the 
problem above: players would ask it what to do. If it is ever tried, it answers only from its own crew's view, under 
these principles, and never about the plan, the manual or the money.
> Docs\DECISIONS.md:1:# DECISIONS.md — decisions taken during implementation
  Docs\DECISIONS.md:2:
  Docs\DECISIONS.md:3:Design decisions live in the design doc (`Docs/DESIGN_v0.md`, "Decisions needed"). This file 
records the smaller calls made while building, so nobody re-litigates them by accident, and the questions that are 
waiting for Bryan. The orchestrator appends; Bryan edits.
