can be table-tested in days; the C# port then has an oracle | `Docs/ORCHESTRATOR.md` |
  Docs\DECISIONS.md:11:| K3 | `rateDrop` is the fraction lost; a crew works at `1 - rateDrop` | Matches the workbook's 
"Base Rate Drop" column | `Data/catalog.json`, `Docs/SCENARIO_SCHEMA.md` |
  Docs\DECISIONS.md:12:| K4 | Authored events always fire; protection changes severity, not likelihood | Stage 2's 
identical seed must meet the same collapse; the catalog's likelihood multipliers are kept for a later random mode | 
scenario `rules.likelihoodRollsApply` |
  Docs\DECISIONS.md:13:| K5 | A trench box is bought for a stretch (from–to) and is in place while the pipe crew works 
inside it; a stretch that misses the collapse station is deviation F3 | Gives Plan a station to name and Site a thing 
to check | `protect` op |
  Docs\DECISIONS.md:14:| K6 | Durations under protection round to the nearest half day | Keeps the arithmetic on the 
front page readable | WO-02 |
  Docs\DECISIONS.md:15:| K7 | A conflict argument fires once per crew pair per stage; afterwards a trailing crew that 
catches its leader idles against it, bills and gets angrier, with no second argument | The foremen have had it out 
once; a re-firing argument would deadlock any plan with one hold | WO-02 |
  Docs\DECISIONS.md:16:| K8 | After a stop-work, any Plan commit lifts it for the zone's crews unless the commit holds 
them | The doc's "stands until Plan commits a plan or resumes" | WO-02 |
  Docs\DECISIONS.md:17:| K9 | Overhead (30%) applies to crew billing and protection daily fees; purchases, 
mobilization, fees and fines at face value | Simplest reading of "30% of direct spend"; the result card shows both | 
