  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:5:## Transport
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:6:
> Docs\PROTOCOL.md:7:- WebSocket, text frames, one JSON object per frame, UTF-8. Path `/ws`. Default port `7331`. The 
host also serves static pages over HTTP on the same port: `/plan.html`, `/site.html`, `/rules.html`, 
`/facilitator.html`.
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:8:- Every message has `"t"` (type) and `"v": 1`. Unknown types are ignored and logged; unknown 
fields are ignored.
> Docs\PROTOCOL.md:9:- The host sends `state` to every client at 4 Hz while the clock runs, and at once after any 
command that changed state. Clients never compute game state; they render.
> Docs\PROTOCOL.md:10:- Times: `day` is a float in simulated days from the stage start (`0.0` = the morning of Day 1; 
the display day is `Math.floor(day) + 1`). `speed` is `"full"` (5 s per day), `"slow"` (20 s per day, during an 
unresolved event), or `"paused"`.
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:11:- Stations: feet from the start of the job as integers; the display form `7+20` means 720 ft. 
Zones are 1-based.
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:12:
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:13:## Client -> host
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:14:
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:30:| op | fields | effect in the simulation |
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:31:| --- | --- | --- |
> Docs\PROTOCOL.md:32:| `setStart` | `crew`, `day` | moves a crew's start day; applies at once; nack `"plan locked"` 
when the plan or the crew is locked, `"crew already started"` after its start |
> Docs\PROTOCOL.md:33:| `hold` | `crew`, `fromDay` (optional, default the order's arrival), `days` (optional; absent = 
until `resume`) | flat segment: the crew stops at the order's arrival and bills while held |
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:34:| `resume` | `crew` | clears a hold or a stop-work on that crew (Site cannot lift a stop-work; 
any Plan commit after a stop-work lifts it for the zone's crews unless the commit holds them) |
> Docs\PROTOCOL.md:35:| `lend` | `machine`, `toCrew`, `days` | the machine leaves its crew at the order's arrival, 
drives along the haul road (same day) and works for `toCrew`, returns after `days`; lending the excavation crew's 
machine to `pipe` during a collapse is the `clear_own` response |
> Docs\PROTOCOL.md:36:| `order` | `machine` (catalog key), `rush`: false | buys a machine: price + $25,000 
mobilization, arrives after lead days (+ city lead delay) |
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:37:| `protect` | `kind` (catalog protection key), `fromFt`, `toFt` | buys protection for a stretch; 
it is in place when the crew working that stretch starts there; wrong stretch = deviation F3 |
> Docs\PROTOCOL.md:38:| `demob` | `crew` | the crew stops billing from the next day; `remob` brings it back after the 
city delay and the fee |
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:39:| `remob` | `crew` | see above |
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:40:| `pay` | `item` (an `options[].key` of an event that is active or whose forecast has landed, 
e.g. `"emergency_shoring"`, `"drainage_pump"`), `machine` (for `hire_excavator`: a catalog key) | pays for a response 
option at once; its effect is the event's authored one; nack `"no such response now"` otherwise |
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:41:| `enterPermit` | `zone`, `code` | opens a zone to excavation if the code matches the zone's 
card; a code not on file -> `nack reason "code not on file"` (a keypad rejection, not a judgement) |
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:42:| `enterInspection` | `zone`, `number` | clears the zone's hold point so backfill may close it |
> Docs\PROTOCOL.md:43:| `radio` | `orderId` | re-sends an order Site reported as not carried out; it lands at once if 
Site is at that crew's station, else next shift; costs nothing but the clock |
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:44:
> Docs\PROTOCOL.md:45:An order (hold, resume, lend, order, protect, demob, remob) becomes an `Order` object with an 
`id`, a `crew`, `issuedDay`, `landsDay` (next shift, or `issuedDay` if the Site client is at that crew's current 
station at commit time), and `status`: `sent`, `landed`, `confirmed`, `notCarriedOut`.
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:46:
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:47:### Site actions
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:48:
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:49:| action | fields | effect |
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:51:| `moveTo` | `stationFt` | the truck drives to the stake; arrival after `|Δft| / 1500` simulated 
hours (one zone per hour of game time; tune later) |
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:52:| `dismount` / `mount` | — | standing at the stake enables `inspect`, `flag`, `stopWork` |
> Docs\PROTOCOL.md:53:| `inspect` | `target`: 
`"wall"|"water"|"pipe"|"machine"|"protection"|"board"|"sky"|"ticket"|"crew"` | the host returns `inspection` with the 
indicator text for that target at Site's station (from the scenario's ground data and current state); reveals hidden 
variants |
> Docs\PROTOCOL.md:54:| `flag` | `stationFt`, `note` (optional, free text ≤ 40 chars) | places an unlabeled marker 
that appears on the Plan page's LOB at that station |
> Docs\PROTOCOL.md:55:| `stopWork` | `zone` | crews in the zone halt within one simulated hour, keep billing, mood 
worsens each day held; stands until Plan commits (a commit lifts it for the zone's crews unless it holds them) |
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:56:| `confirm` | `orderId`, `outcome`: `"done"|"notDone"` | closes the order loop; `notDone` sets 
the order to `notCarriedOut` and appears on Plan's radio log |
> Docs\PROTOCOL.md:57:| `listen` | — | at a conflict or an idle crew, returns the foremen's lines (`voice` with 
`lineIds`) |
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:58:
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:59:## Host -> client
  Docs\PROTOCOL.md:60:
